########################################################
### Testing
########################################################

To test a newly compiled autozmat, type 'make test' at the
shell prompt. Results are compared with authentic files in
Authentic/atomtyping and Authentic/noatomtyping directories.
Then the ratios of successful and failed tests are printed
out at the end.

To test autozmat with atomtyping enabled,
% make test

To test autozmat with atomtyping disabled,
% make test ATOMTYPE_OPT=-a

########################################################
### Usage Examples
########################################################

For help, 
% ../bin/autozmat -h

To create a BOSS Z-matrix for QM/MM calculation from
a MDL MOL format file 'crown.mdl',
% ../bin/autozmat -i mdl < crown.mdl > crown.boss
or
% ../bin/autozmat -i mdl crown.mdl > crown.boss

To create a BOSS Z-matrix for QM/MM calculation from
a MDL MOL format file 'zantac.mdl',
% ../bin/autozmat -i mdl zantac.mdl > zantac.boss

To read a BOSS Z-matrix 'zantac.boss' with parameter
file 'opls.par' and print out a PDB format,
% ../bin/autozmat -i boss -p opls.par zantac.boss > zantac.pdb

To read a MCPRO Z-matrix 'dim.mcpro' with parameter
file 'dim.par' and print out a GAUSSIAN Z-matrix,
% ../bin/autozmat -i mcpro -p dim.par dim.mcpro > dim.gauss

To read a BOSS Z-matrix for QM/MM and print out
Cartesian coordinates, (Note that this does not require
a parameter file)
% ../bin/autozmat -i qm_boss -o xyz crown.boss

To read a Cartesian format file 'benzene.xyz' and add
hydrogens to carbon atoms, then print out a BOSS Z-matrix
for QM/MM calc,
% ../bin/autozmat -i xyz -H benzene.xyz

